Mike Fournier wrote:
> 
> When you mention that there are some more important things to concentrate
> on. Can you possibly elaborate on that. This is my first time playnig
> Nethack. I am doing pretty good so far. I am taking it really slow.  But I'd
> love to know what you meant by that statement.

More important than having a big weapon (IMHO) is having all the
resistances (fire, cold, poison, shock, sleep, disintegration, magic),
free action, reflection, speed, a reliable source of levitation, a
decent AC and a few ways to heal yourself. Even the strongest character
can be instakilled by poison or paralyzed by a gelcube with no chance of
fighting back.
 
> Also, about the ability to have reflection.  If I find or wish for an Amulet
> of Reflection, am I losing out on some other good amulet that I should be
> using instead?

The other good amulets are: magical breathing (quite marginal), ESP
(also comes as a helmet), unchanging (also marginal) and life saving
(not really better than a potion of full healing in most cases).

>  Why is reflection so important to begin with.
> For armor, right now, I have a used a wish to get a Blessed +2 Gray Dragon
> Scale armor.  Now from what I understand, isn't that Dragon Gray Scale Armor
> a magic resist armor? 

Yes

> My understanding of what Reflection does, is that it
> reflects the magic back at the monster.  So the only difference in having
> this Dragon Gray Scale armor instead, is that I'm not reflecting it back,
> but I am fully resisting the magic. Correct?

No. Magic resistance resists _magic_, that is all the nasty touch
attacks of high level spellcasters, the priests' 'open wounds', the psi
bolt spell, wands of death and grey dragon breath. It also saves you
from a few traps, most importantly polymorph traps. Reflection OTOH
reflects all ray- type attacks, that means all dragon breaths and wands.
If you have all the above- mentioned resists, reflection still keeps the
beam from hitting you, so fire- and cold- based ray attacks won't
destroy your inventory (traps and explosions still do). 

> So unless I'm fully missing the point of Reflection, is it really needed?

Nothing is really needed in nethack (except for the Invocation
Artifacts), but to make it short: Reflection is not needed when you have
all the intrinsic resists and put all metal wands/rings/scrolls/potions
things in bags. OTOH when I have the choice (next to never) between
reflection and MR I prefer reflection in the early game because it's
quite satisfactory to see those wand-wielding gnomes shoot themselves.

